# What a created project must not commit. Everything else in here is yours.

# Composer's work, rebuilt by `composer install` from composer.json and the lock.
# The LOCK itself is tracked on purpose: an app pins the versions it was tested
# against. Only a published package ships without one.
/vendor/
/composer.phar

# Secrets. config/.env carries what the environment supplies — SESSION_SECRET, a
# database password, an API token — and docs/sessions-and-csrf.md is explicit
# that the secret stays out of the repository. config/.env.example is the tracked
# template: it names the variables and never their values.
config/.env

# PHPUnit's caches (see cacheDirectory in phpunit.xml.dist).
/.phpunit.cache/
.phpunit.result.cache

# A SQLite database is data, not code: `lava db:migrate` rebuilds the schema, and
# a committed .sqlite file is one developer's rows arriving in everyone's clone.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal

# AGENTS.md is deliberately absent from this list: `lava map` generates it,
# `lava check` fails when it is stale, and keeping it in version control is how a
# reader — human or agent — sees this app's wiring without booting it.
